{
 "turns_text": [
  "[SEG0001] person_1 (CLINICAL_STAFF): Mr Hale? I've put your observations on the screen. Blood pressure is one twenty-eight over seventy-eight, pulse seventy-six, oxygen sats ninety-seven percent, and temperature thirty-six point eight.",
  "[SEG0002] person_2 (PATIENT): Alright.",
  "[SEG0003] person_3 (DOCTOR): Come in. Cough?",
  "[SEG0004] person_2 (PATIENT): Yeah.",
  "[SEG0005] person_3 (DOCTOR): How long?",
  "[SEG0006] person_2 (PATIENT): Six weeks.",
  "[SEG0007] person_3 (DOCTOR): Six weeks after the flu, worse at night?",
  "[SEG0008] person_2 (PATIENT): Yeah.",
  "[SEG0009] person_4 (FAMILY_MEMBER): Every night from about two, mind. And that pay machine ate my coins on the way in, typical.",
  "[SEG0010] person_2 (PATIENT): Not every night.",
  "[SEG0011] person_3 (DOCTOR): Phlegm?",
  "[SEG0012] person_2 (PATIENT): No.",
  "[SEG0013] person_4 (FAMILY_MEMBER): Well, actually, it's green in the mornings. I've seen the tissues.",
  "[SEG0014] person_2 (PATIENT): Dry.",
  "[SEG0015] person_3 (DOCTOR): Any blood?",
  "[SEG0016] person_2 (PATIENT): No.",
  "[SEG0017] person_3 (DOCTOR): Fever?",
  "[SEG0018] person_2 (PATIENT): No.",
  "[SEG0019] person_3 (DOCTOR): Breathless?",
  "[SEG0020] person_2 (PATIENT): No.",
  "[SEG0021] person_3 (DOCTOR): Weight loss?",
  "[SEG0022] person_2 (PATIENT): No.",
  "[SEG0023] person_4 (FAMILY_MEMBER): His trousers are hanging off him. I took the waist in last week.",
  "[SEG0024] person_3 (DOCTOR): Are the clothes loose?",
  "[SEG0025] person_2 (PATIENT): Loose.",
  "[SEG0026] person_3 (DOCTOR): Abroad recently?",
  "[SEG0027] person_2 (PATIENT): No.",
  "[SEG0028] person_3 (DOCTOR): Any contact with TB?",
  "[SEG0029] person_2 (PATIENT): No.",
  "[SEG0030] person_4 (FAMILY_MEMBER): Um, his cousin Darren was poorly around the wedding in March. They were talking about TB. You spoke to him, Colin.",
  "[SEG0031] person_2 (PATIENT): Barely.",
  "[SEG0032] person_3 (DOCTOR): Allergies?",
  "[SEG0033] person_2 (PATIENT): None.",
  "[SEG0034] person_4 (FAMILY_MEMBER): He's on ramipril, ten— well, actually five milligrams by mouth every morning, for his blood pressure. And salbutamol, two puffs, though he hardly uses it.",
  "[SEG0035] person_2 (PATIENT): Rarely.",
  "[SEG0036] person_3 (DOCTOR): Chest is clear, no wheeze. I won't name a cause today. I'm ordering a chest X-ray. Come back when the report's through, or sooner if you cough blood or you're more breathless.",
  "[SEG0037] person_1 (CLINICAL_STAFF): I'll book the X-ray for Thursday and a review the following week. Mind the step, it's wet."
 ],
